Found during k75 (worker), confirmed by the orchestrator. GitSource.resolve runs `git fetch --depth 1 origin <ref>` (src/sources/git.ts ~81-87) with the configured ref unvalidated (config.ts). git still parses options after the remote name, so ref `--upload-pack=<cmd>` runs <cmd> (worker reproduced in a scratch repo). Trust (state.ts isTrusted) binds only kind+address, NOT the ref: a project config (a cloned repo) whose source the user trusted can later change that source's ref to an option and get command execution at the next SessionStart without any new trust prompt. Also harden the url: a url starting with "-" in ls-remote/clone/remote add, and probe.ts `git ls-remote <baseUrl>`. Fix: reject a ref or git url starting with "-" at config load (clear error naming the source), AND pass `--end-of-options` (or `--` where git supports it) before every user-supplied positional in git invocations (fetch, ls-remote, clone/remote add, probe) as defence in depth; check the minimum git version skilletor documents supports --end-of-options (git 2.24+) or pick a form that works on older git. Tests: config rejects ref/url with leading "-"; a direct GitSource call with such a ref never runs the injected command (e.g. --upload-pack=touch <marker> → marker absent); runHook with a trusted project source whose ref turns into an option → no marker, a warning, exit 0.

